            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good recipe. Easy to prepare, Flavorful and quick.",
            "datePublished": "2021-05-20T11:13:31.463Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Christine"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My husband and I really like this. Here's what I do differently:\n-I like to use dehydrated onion, because I don't like a lot of crunch (only do 3 Tbsp, I don't know why it's listed twice in the ingredient list).\n-This tastes good with either canned or leftover chicken.\n-I use raw spinach instead of cooked, and I don't really measure it, I just rip it up and add it in step 2. This also works really well with frozen spinach, because it's a lot faster to break up.\n-I use 2 eggs instead of 1, and I cut them up into small pieces and crumble the yolk into the mixture, instead of having it in slices like it shows in the picture.\n*Note: I found that this makes enough for 5 slices of bread.",
            "datePublished": "2016-10-20T19:46:00.940Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
